    * parameters: ('- Brand Name & Identity Direction: Exploring various naming directions (European/Latin roots, direct/descriptive, sensory/wellness, and warm/artisanal local styles) to establish an authentic brand vibe that aligns with the mid-to-high artisanal pricing tier.\n- Tiered Retail Pricing Strategy:\n  - Mini Jar / Travel Tin (~100g): EGP 200 - 250 (low barrier to entry for testing and giveaways).\n  - Standard Jar (~180-200g): EGP 380 - 480 (core high-margin personal/gifting item).\n  - Large / Double Wick Jar (~300-350g): EGP 600 - 750 (smart local alternative to high-end imported luxury brands).\n- Advertising & Launch Campaign Strategy:\n  - Funnel Structure: Split into a 2-week Teaser Phase (35% budget allocation focusing on brand awareness, waitlists, and creative testing) and a Launch Phase (65% budget allocation utilizing Carousel and Video ads for direct conversion).\n  - Ad Angles: Emphasize clean-burning health benefits (soy vs. paraffin), sustainable upcycled glass decor utility, and attainable luxury scent profiles.\n  - Budget Scenarios: Ranging from Lean Launch (EGP 5,000 - 7,500), Balanced Growth / Recommended (EGP 12,000 - 15,000), to Aggressive / Scale (EGP 25,000 - 35,000) for the launch month targeting urban centers in Cairo, Giza, and Alexandria.\n  - Creative Execution: Prioritize video-first content (Reels showcasing mood lighting, melting soy, and crackling wicks) alongside rapid inbox response management.', {'active_plans': '- Brand Name & Identity Direction: Exploring various naming directions (European/Latin roots, direct/descriptive, sensory/wellness, and warm/artisanal local styles) to establish an authentic brand vibe that aligns with the mid-to-high artisanal pricing tier.\n- Tiered Retail Pricing Strategy:\n  - Mini Jar / Travel Tin (~100g): EGP 200 - 250 (low barrier to entry for testing and giveaways).\n  - Standard Jar (~180-200g): EGP 380 - 480 (core high-margin personal/gifting item).\n  - Large / Double Wick Jar (~300-350g): EGP 600 - 750 (smart local alternative to high-end imported luxury brands).\n- Advertising & Launch Campaign Strategy:\n  - Funnel Structure: Split into a 2-week Teaser Phase (35% budget allocation focusing on brand awareness, waitlists, and creative testing) and a Launch Phase (65% budget allocation utilizing Carousel and Video ads for direct conversion).\n  - Ad Angles: Emphasize clean-burning health benefits (soy vs. paraffin), sustainable upcycled glass decor utility, and attainable luxury scent profiles.\n  - Budget Scenarios: Ranging from Lean Launch (EGP 5,000 - 7,500), Balanced Growth / Recommended (EGP 12,000 - 15,000), to Aggressive / Scale (EGP 25,000 - 35,000) for the launch month targeting urban centers in Cairo, Giza, and Alexandria.\n  - Creative Execution: Prioritize video-first content (Reels showcasing mood lighting, melting soy, and crackling wicks) alongside rapid inbox response management.', 'source': 'ltm_compressor', 'created_at': '2026-10-11T20:11:09.435131+00:00', 'updated_at': '2026-10-12T10:23:08.880097+00:00'}, 'mem_plan_ba3c879d057b')
