    * parameters: ('- Brand Name: Unnamed (Planning stage / Name selection phase)\n- Industry/Sector: Scented and Decorative Candles / Home Fragrance (Focused on clean-burning soy wax, classical cotton wicks, and heavy-duty, heat-resistant glass containers engineered for multi-cycle home decor upcycling)\n- Geography/Country: Egypt (with primary urban fulfillment and target zones including Cairo, Giza, and Alexandria, specifically targeting high-end residential hubs like New Cairo, 5th Settlement, Sheikh Zayed, 6th of October, Maadi, and Smouha)\n- Target Audience: Urban home decor enthusiasts, fragrance lovers, wellness seekers, and health-conscious consumers desiring attainable luxury, emotional wellness, sensory escapism, mental restoration, and pride in local artisanal craftsmanship\n- Pricing Policy & Architecture: Segmented across structured market tiers:\n  - Entry-level/Mass: EGP 300 to 350 (represented by regional legacy operators like Flamingo and Areej Aromatherapy)\n  - Lower-Middle Tier: EGP 382 to 590 (represented by indie brands like Bubblzz, LOCKEN, and Aromatica)\n  - Mid-to-High Artisanal Void/Sweet Spot (Target Tier): EGP 600 to 850 (unexploited quality tier bridging basic indie alternatives and luxury pricing)\n  - Luxury: Up to EGP 950+ (represented by regional indie brand Pia Scents; benchmarked against international giants like Bath & Body Works, where large 3-Wick candles reach EGP 1,200 to 1,400+)\n- Known Competitors & Market Players: Bath & Body Works, Egyptian and regional multi-brand marketplaces and indie brands including Source Beauty, Pia Scents, Bubblzz, Areej Aromatherapy, Flamingo, Splendour, LOCKEN, and Aromatica\n- Product Assortment Characteristics & Whitespaces: Premium soy wax compositions (avoiding toxic, headache-inducing paraffin), clean aesthetic profiles, prolonged burn times, diverse scent architectures spanning warm vanilla, soothing lavender, pumpkin cinnamon, fresh linen, and sophisticated regional oud blends combined with local botanicals. Critical structural whitespaces include reusable upcycled glass vessels, corporate gifting and boutique hospitality private-label programs for spas and hotels, seasonal limited-edition collections, and curated quarterly sensory subscription box frameworks to prevent consumer brand fatigue', UUID('bd10c9c7-9809-4016-954c-d0bc434fc638'))
